Review these previously model-flagged conflict pairs against the supplied quotations and scope/date fields. Do not assume every pair is a conflict. Different products, origins, tariff programs, or dated stages are not automatically contradictory. Only use apparent_same_scope_conflict when the supplied claims appear incompatible on the same scope/date; otherwise distinguish dated progression, differing scope, complementary claims, and missing scope. Do not verify current law from memory. Explain the reason briefly for every pair.
UNTRUSTED_EVIDENCE_JSON:
{"research_date": "2026-09-10", "pairs": [{"pair_id": "conflict_e849cc22ac9a2ee1c873e778", "claim_ids": ["claim_0f9fcb863cf90559e90eccad", "claim_d657e93da637a61c8c10690c"], "query_ids": ["q_242"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_0f9fcb863cf90559e90eccad", "quote": "The duty provided in heading 9903.94.05 is in addition to any special rate of duty under a free trade agreement or preference program listed in general note 3(c)(i) to the tariff schedule, except as provided for in subdivision (h) of U.S. note 33 to subchapter III of chapter 99 of the HTSUS.", "url": "https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDHSCBP/bulletins/3de7ef9", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_d657e93da637a61c8c10690c", "quote": "Yes, parts of automobiles that qualify for preferential tariff treatment under USMCA, self-certified by importers to be used for automobile production or repair activity in the United States, are eligible to use HTS 9903.94.06.", "url": "https://www.cbp.gov/trade/programs-administration/entry-summary/section-232-additional-faqs-autos", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "USMCA", "affected_product": "parts of automobiles", "hts_code": "9903.94.06"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_5ca8aa4a5572050f334fb135", "claim_ids": ["claim_a28cf5fb8e0a8dab4fa13469", "claim_cb029ce235aafafc634fd769"], "query_ids": ["q_242"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_a28cf5fb8e0a8dab4fa13469", "quote": "No drawback is available with respect to the additional duties imposed pursuant to the Presidential Proclamation 10908, as implemented in the FRN 90 FR 14705.", "url": "https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDHSCBP/bulletins/3de7ef9", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_cb029ce235aafafc634fd769", "quote": "For automobile parts from Japan, South Korea, Taiwan, the UK, and the member countries of the EU (Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Croatia, Cyprus, Czechia (Czech Republic), Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Ireland, Italy, Latvia, Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta, Netherlands, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Slovakia, Slovenia, Spain, Sweden), the additional tariff for automobile parts is calculated based on the difference between the column one duty rate and the 232 duty rate.", "url": "https://www.ghy.com/trade-compliance/us-to-apply-a-25-tariff-on-imports-of-autos-and-parts", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_de885368d1f8b3907d615ded", "claim_ids": ["claim_2dc224d6876a1e0cde999f62", "claim_34dc8aa7c7efd881491b19fa"], "query_ids": ["q_243"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_2dc224d6876a1e0cde999f62", "quote": "Other factors include section 232 steel and aluminum tariffs already implemented, the other 232 tariffs proposed, section 301 tariffs proposed that since this time have now come into effect", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "section 232 steel and aluminum tariffs", "legal_authority": "section 232", "reported_policy_status": "already implemented"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_34dc8aa7c7efd881491b19fa", "quote": "Unfortunately, none of the tariff lines listed below were removed from the announced tariffs and, barring approval of exemption requests or action by congress, we will face the full and onerous impact of these tariffs.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"reported_policy_status": "announced tariffs"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_6789389a3c555e0157ee2c40", "claim_ids": ["claim_1c8e30cc3fdb762f58391784", "claim_266dae3c15241cf4221c22f4"], "query_ids": ["q_243"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_1c8e30cc3fdb762f58391784", "quote": "the price of a new vehicle in the range of $1,400 to $7,000 per vehicle.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"duty_rate": "$1,400 to $7,000"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_266dae3c15241cf4221c22f4", "quote": "The American Automotive Policy Council estimates steel and aluminum tariffs will cause a $400 per-car price increase.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "steel and aluminum tariffs", "duty_rate": "$400 per-car price increase"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_3c5d98d197c117e1a5023d48", "claim_ids": ["claim_040e85c79e17b110585e15d7", "claim_2b7cd1b433c890bb33dcf1c8"], "query_ids": ["q_243"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_040e85c79e17b110585e15d7", "quote": "The car study that I mentioned earlier predicts that new car dealerships would see a loss of at least 117,000 jobs and a loss of as much as $66.5 billion in revenue if a 25-percent tariff is implemented.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"duty_rate": "25-percent tariff"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_2b7cd1b433c890bb33dcf1c8", "quote": "The number of jobs lost in other industries as a direct consequence of these tariffs has been calculated at 250,000 resulting in a net loss of 158,000 American jobs when accounting for estimated employment gains in the auto and parts sectors.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_83dd178a7e7237e2f820ebd6", "claim_ids": ["claim_266dae3c15241cf4221c22f4", "claim_2a16231407701d08010ebdfe"], "query_ids": ["q_243"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_266dae3c15241cf4221c22f4", "quote": "The American Automotive Policy Council estimates steel and aluminum tariffs will cause a $400 per-car price increase.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "steel and aluminum tariffs", "duty_rate": "$400 per-car price increase"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_2a16231407701d08010ebdfe", "quote": "Senator Portman. Mr. Haughey, you make a lot of stuff in Ohio too. It is more parts, and we appreciate your suppliers, your companies in Ohio. Talk to us about what the cost to the car is going to be. We have a $2,000 increase on average for a domestically produced car.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Mr. Haughey"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_598bbb128ae8c7900d42ce4b", "claim_ids": ["claim_267d59b60a01e97cb3bd905f", "claim_2932ae5f4faa5974a5196f0d"], "query_ids": ["q_243"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_267d59b60a01e97cb3bd905f", "quote": "More than 90 percent of the steel we use to produce our vehicles here is sourced here in America. So we are paying direct tariffs on the less than 10 percent that we import.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Honda North America"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_2932ae5f4faa5974a5196f0d", "quote": "At other Honda plants in Georgia and Ohio, we build high-tech transmissions using very precise and advanced technologies.", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg40897/html/CHRG-115shrg40897.htm", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Honda", "facility": "Honda plants in Georgia"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_28e0d756e6f6f687f897e61c", "claim_ids": ["claim_02c0a159872d5a6a51639ca6", "claim_275c05d186b10cfc69491626"], "query_ids": ["q_244"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_02c0a159872d5a6a51639ca6", "quote": "If assembly takes place in Mexico, an additional 25 percent tariff under the IEEPA would apply unless the EVs qualify as USMCA-originating goods.", "url": "https://scholarship.law.duke.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1618&context=djcil", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "IEEPA", "duty_rate": "25 percent"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_275c05d186b10cfc69491626", "quote": "automakers produce EVs outside China—such as in Mexico or elsewhere—where the STT is satisfied. In such cases, the 100 percent tariff under Section 301 may be avoided, although the vehicle would remain subject to the 25 percent tariff under Section 232.", "url": "https://scholarship.law.duke.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1618&context=djcil", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301", "duty_rate": "100 percent"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_9275a22ca4fd65aab5f7fcf0", "claim_ids": ["claim_43a6b60c8646d24ae10b8a8b", "claim_c8395b727700d0db203a2a95"], "query_ids": ["q_244"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_43a6b60c8646d24ae10b8a8b", "quote": "In practical terms, it appears that an OEM assembling vehicles in Mexico (or any other country) may source components from Chinese suppliers without triggering Section 301 tariffs, as long as those components are not imported under a CKD logistics structure.", "url": "https://scholarship.law.duke.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1618&context=djcil", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_c8395b727700d0db203a2a95", "quote": "an OEM assembling vehicles in Mexico (or any other country) may source components from Chinese suppliers without triggering Section 301 tariffs, as long as those components are not imported under a CKD logistics structure.", "url": "https://scholarship.law.duke.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1618&context=djcil", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_9cb3b44ede21e6872626da80", "claim_ids": ["claim_26b5d58dc736d5cb6c27c98a", "claim_9cef2271ef92b9cbe35f6ffe"], "query_ids": ["q_245"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_26b5d58dc736d5cb6c27c98a", "quote": "President Trump expands steel and aluminum tariffs to all countries; effective March 12, 2025", "url": "https://www.oxfordenergy.org/wpcms/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/OEF-144.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "steel and aluminum tariffs", "legal_authority": "President Trump", "effective_date": "March 12, 2025"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_9cef2271ef92b9cbe35f6ffe", "quote": "President Trump has threatened to impose a 25 per cent tariff on all Mexican imports, including all cars that are not manufactured in the US, unless Mexico curbs illegal migration and drug trafficking.", "url": "https://www.oxfordenergy.org/wpcms/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/OEF-144.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "President Trump", "tariff_program": "25 per cent tariff on all Mexican imports, including all cars that are not manufactured in the US"}}]}]}

